{"id":"rdb-d6a593","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Support DATE, TIME, DATETIME, and TIMESTAMP types","description":"Add temporal SQL types to RepoDB's type system.\n\nRequires changes to:\n- `decodeType()` — map `Type_DATE`, `Type_TIME`, `Type_DATETIME`, `Type_TIMESTAMP` to go-mysql-server types\n- `rawValue()` — serialize `time.Time` (DATE/DATETIME/TIMESTAMP) and timespan (TIME) to bytes\n- `decodeRow()` — deserialize stored bytes back to Go values\n- `encodeKey()` — support temporal types as primary key columns\n- `sqlLiteral()` — bind `time.Time` parameters\n- Tests: DDL, insert/select round-trip, ordering, persistence through reopen, parameter binding","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"rdb-e45ce6","estimate":2,"sort_order":"a1","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T12:28:08.802457Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-6c79e3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Support DECIMAL and NUMERIC types","description":"Add fixed-point decimal types to RepoDB's type system.\n\ngo-mysql-server uses `decimal.Decimal` from shopspring/decimal. DECIMAL(precision, scale) needs precision and scale persisted in `columnDisk`.\n\nRequires changes to:\n- `columnDisk` — add precision/scale fields\n- `decodeType()` — map `Type_DECIMAL` with precision/scale\n- `encodeSchema()`/`decodeSchema()` — persist precision and scale\n- `rawValue()` / `decodeRow()` — serialize/deserialize `decimal.Decimal`\n- `sqlLiteral()` — bind decimal parameters\n- Tests: DDL, round-trip, arithmetic, ordering, persistence","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"rdb-e45ce6","estimate":2,"sort_order":"a2","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T12:28:12.064356Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-ef5811","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Support ENUM type","description":"Add ENUM type to RepoDB's type system.\n\nENUM requires storing the list of allowed values in the schema. go-mysql-server's `CreateEnumType(values, collation)` returns a type that stores values as uint16 indices internally.\n\nRequires changes to:\n- `columnDisk` — add enum values field\n- `decodeType()` — create ENUM type with stored values\n- `encodeSchema()`/`decodeSchema()` — persist enum values\n- `rawValue()` / `decodeRow()` — serialize/deserialize enum values (uint16 index)\n- Tests: DDL, insert valid/invalid values, round-trip, ordering, persistence","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"rdb-e45ce6","estimate":1,"sort_order":"a3","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T12:28:15.833046Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-160131","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Support native JSON type","description":"Add native JSON type to RepoDB's type system (currently JSON data can only be stored as TEXT).\n\ngo-mysql-server has `types.JSON` (`JsonType{}`) which uses `sql.JSONDocument`. This enables JSON functions and proper JSON validation.\n\nRequires changes to:\n- `decodeType()` — map `Type_JSON` to `types.JSON`\n- `rawValue()` / `decodeRow()` — serialize/deserialize JSON documents\n- Tests: DDL, insert/select round-trip, JSON functions, persistence","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"rdb-e45ce6","estimate":1,"sort_order":"a4","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T12:28:19.309263Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-cab03f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Support collation-aware string comparisons","description":"Add collation support for string columns, at minimum `utf8mb4_general_ci` for case-insensitive comparisons.\n\nCurrently all strings use `sql.Collation_Default`. This requires:\n- `columnDisk` — add collation field\n- `encodeSchema()`/`decodeSchema()` — persist collation\n- `decodeType()` — pass collation to `types.CreateString()`\n- `table.Collation()` — return table-level collation\n- Tests: case-insensitive WHERE, ORDER BY, UNIQUE constraints with collation","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"rdb-e45ce6","estimate":2,"sort_order":"a5","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T12:28:22.806332Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
