{"id":"rdb-6c79e3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-165ff918-3c43-4815-a01e-5d7152f37e1a","text":"Implementation complete. All tests pass (full suite, zero regressions).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n`engine/catalog.go`:\n- `columnDisk` — added `Scale` field (omitempty for backward compat)\n- `encodeSchema()` — extracts precision/scale from `sql.DecimalType`\n- `decodeSchema()` — passes scale to `decodeType()`\n- `decodeType()` — added `scale` parameter; handles `Type_DECIMAL` via `types.CreateColumnDecimalType(precision, scale)` with default precision=10 for bare `DECIMAL`\n- `validateSchema()` — extracts and passes decimal precision/scale\n- `rawValue()` — serializes `decimal.Decimal` via `d.String()`\n- `decodeRow()` — deserializes via `decimal.NewFromString()` then `Convert()` for bounds/rounding\n- Added `github.com/shopspring/decimal` import (already a transitive dep)\n\n`engine/engine.go`:\n- `sqlLiteral()` — handles `decimal.Decimal` as bare numeric literal\n- Added `github.com/shopspring/decimal` import\n\n`engine/engine_test.go`:\n- 8 new tests with exact value assertions: DDL (DECIMAL + NUMERIC), bare DECIMAL, round-trip (99.99, 0.1, 12345678.5), arithmetic (price × qty = 59.97), ORDER BY, nullable, persistence through reopen, DEFAULT values\n\nNo decisions diverged from the spec."},"created_at":"2026-09-14T15:43:22.549482Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
