{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-67eb5edb-e7fe-4fa4-a797-8037738fffcf","text":"Implementation complete. 803 lines across 7 files.\n\n**Core changes:**\n\n`common/repository/repository.go`:\n- Added `Indexes map[string]storage.Hash` to `Table` struct for index tree root persistence\n- Added `Table.Equal()` method (map field makes Table non-comparable with `==`)\n\n`engine/catalog.go` (main implementation):\n- `indexDisk` struct for schema persistence (name, column ordinals, unique flag)\n- `schemaDisk` extended with `Indexes []indexDisk`\n- `encodeSchema`/`decodeSchema` updated for new signatures\n- `tableState` gains `indexes []indexDisk` and `idxEdits map[string][]prolly.Edit`\n- `encodeIndexKey()` — builds binary keys from arbitrary columns with NULL handling (PK appended as disambiguator for NULL != NULL semantics) and collation weight strings\n- `lookupIndexKey()` — checks pending edits then persisted prolly tree\n- `ensureIndexEdits()` — rebuilds in-memory index edits from existing rows when index tree hasn't been persisted (critical for journal/typed-edits path)\n- `editor.Insert/Update/Delete` — uniqueness enforcement with index edit maintenance\n- `commitIndexTrees()` / `buildIndexTreeForDef()` — builds or applies index trees at commit time\n- `commitNativeGit` — wires index trees into both existing-data and new-table paths\n- `CreateIndex` / `DropIndex` / `RenameIndex` — `sql.IndexAlterableTable` implementation\n- `uniqueIndex` type — `sql.Index` implementation with point-equality support\n- `GetIndexes()` returns unique indexes alongside primary index\n- `cachedTableMeta` extended with indexes\n\n`engine/merge.go`:\n- `rebuildIndexesFromTree()` — scans merged data tree to rebuild index trees, detects uniqueness violations\n- `copyTable` includes index tree objects in reachable set\n\n**9 new tests covering:**\n- DDL (CREATE TABLE with UNIQUE, ALTER TABLE ADD UNIQUE, DROP INDEX)\n- Enforcement (INSERT duplicate rejected, UPDATE to duplicate rejected)\n- NULL semantics (multiple NULLs allowed)\n- Composite unique (multi-column)\n- Collation (case-insensitive unique under utf8mb4_general_ci)\n- Persistence (survives close/reopen)\n- ALTER TABLE ADD rejects existing duplicates\n\n**Key design decision not in the original spec:** The typed-edits (journal) path needed special handling — `ensureIndexEdits` rebuilds index entries from existing rows when the index tree hasn't been checkpointed yet. This ensures uniqueness enforcement works across auto-commits in the journal path without extending the journal format.\n\nFull test suite passes."},"created_at":"2026-09-15T09:57:44.142493Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-854d115b-79d4-463c-b728-70dbc08cf02f","text":"All five P1 issues fixed with regression tests:\n\n**P1-1: Journal-mode DDL discards data** — `working.go:459` was replacing the entire `Table` descriptor when only the schema changed. Fixed: now preserves `DataRoot` and `Indexes` by reading the existing entry and updating only `SchemaRoot`. Regression test: `TestUniqueIndexJournalDDLPreservesData`.\n\n**P1-2: Unique index lookups routed to primary key** — `LookupPartitions` always used PK ordinals. Fixed: split into `lookupPrimaryPartitions` and `lookupUniquePartitions`. The latter encodes the index key, resolves it to a PK via `resolveIndexToPK` (checks edits then tree), then looks up the row by PK. Regression test: existing tests pass; `GetIndexes` now correctly serves optimizer lookups.\n\n**P1-3: Column alterations leave index ordinals stale** — `AddColumn` and `DropColumn` adjusted PK ordinals but not index ordinals. Fixed: both methods now remap `indexDisk.Columns` with the same shift logic as PK ordinals. `DropColumn` rejects dropping a column used by an index. `ModifyColumn` with FIRST/AFTER also remaps index ordinals. All three clear `idxEdits` to force rebuild. Regression tests: `TestUniqueAddColumnPreservesIndex`, `TestUniqueDropIndexedColumnRejected`.\n\n**P1-4: Multiple edits to one index key fail commit** — Valid transactions (delete row, insert different PK with same unique value) produced duplicate keys in the edit slice. Fixed: added `coalesceEdits()` that deduplicates by keeping only the last edit per key before sorting. Regression test: `TestUniqueDeleteThenInsertSameValue`.\n\n**P1-5: Failed statements don't roll back index edits** — `DiscardChanges` restored row state but not `idxEdits`. Fixed: `StatementBegin` snapshots `idxEdits`; `DiscardChanges` restores the snapshot. Regression test: `TestUniqueIndexRollbackOnFailedStatement`.\n\nFull suite passes (14 unique constraint tests total)."},"created_at":"2026-09-15T10:50:01.340044Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T12:49:54.943841Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-265f08f8-a5c1-49c7-a356-5a691912edb0","text":"Second review fixes complete. Spec updated per workflow. Four P1s addressed:\n\n**P1-1: Native-Git commits discard index objects for unchanged tables** — `ValidateSnapshot` now includes index tree hashes in the per-table object cache (engine.go:162-168). The `commitNativeGit` unchanged-table path already trusted this cache, so index objects are now retained. Regression test: `TestUniqueConstraintNativeGitMultiTable` — creates table with UNIQUE + data, reopens, modifies a different table, verifies unique constraint still enforced.\n\n**P1-2: Journal checkpoints don't materialize index trees** — Added `checkpointIndexTrees` (engine.go) that decodes the schema, gets index definitions, and calls `rebuildIndexesFromTree` to build index trees from the checkpointed data tree. Both existing-data and new-table branches now include index roots in the table descriptor. Regression test: `TestUniqueConstraintPersistsThroughReopen` (journal mode, which is the default).\n\n**P1-3: PK-changing update leaves stale index values** — In `Update`, when `oldIdxKey == newIdxKey` but `oldKey != newKey`, now emits an edit to update the index value (which stores the PK). Regression test: `TestUniquePKChangeUpdatesIndexValue` — updates PK from 1 to 10, verifies unique-index lookup returns the new PK.\n\n**P1-4: ModifyColumn type change doesn't rebuild index** — After type conversion, if the changed column participates in a unique index, re-encodes all index keys and checks for collapsed uniqueness violations. Clears `idxEdits` to force rebuild. Regression test: `TestUniqueModifyColumnTypeCollapse` — changes VARCHAR '01'/'1' to BIGINT (both become 1), expects rejection.\n\nAdditionally:\n- 6 new tests (3 native-git, 1 PK update, 1 type collapse, 1 multi-table retention) bringing total to 20\n- Spec updated with all review-driven revisions\n\nFull suite passes."},"created_at":"2026-09-15T12:50:09.913389Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T12:58:40.132045Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-151bccfc-ac02-4122-8a8a-329952babac9","text":"Third review fixes complete. Spec updated. Three P1s addressed:\n\n**P1-1: Journal checkpoints can't publish schema changes to existing tables** — `checkpointTypedEdits` (engine.go:267) now copies the schema object to the checkpoint writer whenever the schema hash differs from the base table's, not just for new tables. Regression test: `TestUniqueJournalCheckpointWithDDL` — creates table + data, reopens, adds UNIQUE index, reopens again, verifies data preserved and index enforced.\n\n**P1-2: Type change reuses old index tree** — After validating uniqueness, `ModifyColumn` now deletes the affected index roots from `state.manifest.Indexes` (catalog.go), forcing `commitIndexTrees` to rebuild via `buildIndexTreeForDef` instead of the \"valid root + no edits = reuse\" path. Regression test: `TestUniqueModifyColumnTypeRebuildIndex` — changes VARCHAR to BIGINT (non-collapsing), verifies uniqueness still enforced after the type change.\n\n**P1-3: Rejected type conversion corrupts shared metadata cache** — Two fixes: (a) Cache-hit path now deep-clones the schema via `copySchema` (catalog.go:175) so transaction-level mutations can't leak back. (b) `ModifyColumn` builds a candidate schema and converts values into a temporary map, checks uniqueness against the candidate, and only mutates `state.schema` and `state.rows` if all validation passes. Regression test: `TestUniqueModifyColumnRejectionDoesNotCorruptCache` — rejects collapsing ALTER, verifies a subsequent session still reads the original VARCHAR values.\n\n23 tests total, full suite passes."},"created_at":"2026-09-15T12:58:53.570221Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ccc98806-0750-4658-9be2-eb3502231052","text":"Fourth review fix complete.\n\n**P1: Schema-only journal checkpoints omit changed schema** — Two fixes:\n\n1. `PendingEdits()` (working.go:483) now includes tables with schema data even when they have no row edits (`te.schemaData != nil`). This ensures `Checkpoint` routes them through `checkpointTypedEdits` instead of taking the no-pending shortcut.\n\n2. `checkpointTypedEdits` (engine.go:249) now detects tables whose schema hash differs from the base but have no pending row edits (`!hasPending \u0026\u0026 schemaChanged`). For these, it copies the schema object to the writer, retains the existing data tree objects, and rebuilds index trees.\n\n**Regression test fixed**: `TestUniqueJournalCheckpointWithDDL` now explicitly calls `eng.Checkpoint()` after both the initial data and the ALTER TABLE ADD UNIQUE, then reopens in native-git mode to verify the checkpointed state. This exercises the actual checkpoint codepath, not just journal replay.\n\nFull suite passes, 23 tests."},"created_at":"2026-09-15T13:20:06.794729Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-47263ff0-d695-44db-8145-6974e8e9eff6","text":"Fifth review fix complete.\n\n**P1: Rolling back first indexed statement loses rebuilt baseline** — `StatementBegin` now calls `ensureIndexEdits` before snapshotting, so the baseline is populated with real data rather than capturing a nil→empty-map transition. After rollback, `DiscardChanges` restores the populated map and subsequent statements correctly find pre-existing entries.\n\n**Regression test rewritten**: `TestUniqueIndexRollbackOnFailedStatement` now uses an explicit transaction (`s.Begin`), fails a multi-row insert within it, then within the same transaction verifies both that (a) duplicating a pre-existing value is still rejected (proves the baseline survived the rollback) and (b) the rolled-back value is insertable (proves phantom entries were cleaned up).\n\nFull suite passes, 23 tests."},"created_at":"2026-09-15T20:52:33.744032Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3e44c189-2919-44fb-872c-16e957e8b6db","text":"Sixth review fixes complete.\n\n**P1: StatementBegin discards index init errors** — `StatementBegin` now stores the `ensureIndexEdits` error in `editor.idxInitErr`. `Insert` and `Update` check this at the top and return it immediately, preventing any bypass of uniqueness enforcement after a failed initialization.\n\n**P2: Index metadata shallow-copied between transactions** — Added `copyIndexes` (deep-clones `[]indexDisk` including backing `Columns` slices) and `copyManifestIndexes` (clones `map[string]storage.Hash`). Cache-hit path now uses both, so `RenameIndex` mutating the slice and type changes deleting from `manifest.Indexes` cannot leak across transactions.\n\n**Test fix**: `TestUniqueIndexRollbackOnFailedStatement` now unconditionally asserts the invalid multi-row insert fails (no `if err != nil` guard). All three post-rollback assertions (invalid insert rejected, pre-existing duplicate still rejected, rolled-back value insertable) execute on every run.\n\nFull suite passes, 23 tests."},"created_at":"2026-09-16T11:48:38.837188Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T12:13:21.181539Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-9fd1c1d1-4568-42a8-b2d6-f96b53cf35d9","text":"Seventh review fixes complete. Spec updated.\n\n**P1: Failed init disables future index initialization** — `StatementBegin` now returns early on `ensureIndexEdits` failure *before* building the snapshot. `idxSnapshot` stays nil, so `DiscardChanges` doesn't touch `idxEdits` — preserving the nil rebuild signal. `Delete` now also checks `idxInitErr` alongside Insert and Update.\n\n**P2: Cache-miss transactions share mutable metadata with cache** — The cache-miss path now deep-clones schema (`copySchema`), indexes (`copyIndexes`), and manifest indexes (`copyManifestIndexes`) when storing to `newCache`. The transaction keeps the original objects; the cache gets independent copies. This matches the cache-hit path's isolation guarantees.\n\nFull suite passes, 23 tests."},"created_at":"2026-09-16T12:13:30.45724Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0777da57-fdfa-4069-889b-0ef0ed140afb","text":"Eighth review fix: `ensureIndexEdits` now builds into a local map and assigns `s.idxEdits` only after the full scan succeeds. A mid-scan failure leaves `s.idxEdits` nil, preserving the rebuild signal. Full suite passes."},"created_at":"2026-09-16T12:22:49.037443Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a1f9d1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-29ae106d-9dc8-4f45-b373-9cdccb6e3a0c","text":"Audit-driven fixes complete. Three changes:\n\n1. **`loadTableMetadata` clones `manifest.Indexes`** — the map from the snapshot is now deep-cloned via `copyManifestIndexes`, so ModifyColumn's `delete(t.state.manifest.Indexes, ...)` can't mutate the snapshot's shared map.\n\n2. **`ensureIndexEdits` always initializes `idxEdits` when indexes exist** — when all indexes are persisted (native-git mode after commit), it now sets `idxEdits = make(...)` instead of returning early with nil. This prevents the panic from `addIndexEdit` when `Insert`/`Update`/`Delete` append edits in a transaction where all trees were already committed.\n\n3. **Dead code cleaned up** — `addIndexEdit`'s nil guard replaced with a panic (catches programming errors). `RenameIndex`'s unreachable nil check removed.\n\nThe panic in fix 2 exposed a real bug the audit flagged as \"unreachable\" — it was unreachable in journal mode but fired in native-git mode where indexes ARE persisted. This validates the audit approach while showing that \"unreachable in current tests\" ≠ \"unreachable.\"\n\nFull suite passes, 23 tests."},"created_at":"2026-09-16T12:28:05.405981Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
