{"id":"rdb-3c8ef9","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-790f4c03-3841-45bb-a5aa-d68dcaeba92a","text":"Implementation complete. Changes:\n\n**`cmd/repodb/main.go`** — Added `promptCheckpointIfDirty` function and wired it into the `sync` case:\n- Before calling `integration.Sync`, checks if stdin is a TTY via `golang.org/x/term.IsTerminal`\n- If TTY and journal is dirty: prompts on stderr with `Journal has uncommitted changes at generation N. Checkpoint before syncing? [y/N]`\n- On `y`/`Y`: runs checkpoint with message `\"checkpoint before sync\"`, prints commit hash to stderr, then proceeds with sync\n- On anything else (including EOF): returns the same `ErrWorkingDirty` error as the non-interactive path\n- If no TTY: skips the prompt entirely, `integration.Sync` handles the error as before\n\n**`go.mod` / `go.sum`** — Added `golang.org/x/term v0.46.0` (upgraded `golang.org/x/sys` to v0.48.0 as transitive dep).\n\nNo changes to `integration/integration.go` — `Sync()` and `requireCleanWorkingState()` remain untouched. All existing tests pass."},"created_at":"2026-09-17T16:10:46.455749Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.274 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
