{"id":"rdb-6e40a9","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-c263f754-c4ca-4145-9d01-0b8d2d4c4a3d","text":"Implementation ready for review.\n\n**Changes**\n- New package `common/robustio`:\n  - `robustio.go`: a cross-platform `retry` loop modeled on Go's `cmd/internal/robustio`. It starts at 1ms with jittered, roughly doubling backoff, is bounded at 2s total, and returns the last error.\n  - `robustio_windows.go`: `Rename`/`Remove` retry on `ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED` / `ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION`, matched with `errors.As` through `*os.LinkError`/`*os.PathError`.\n  - `robustio_other.go` (`!windows`): plain `os.Rename`/`os.Remove`, with no retry.\n- Call sites: `saveConflictSet` rename and `clearConflictSet` remove in `integration/conflicts.go`, and `Filesystem.Put` rename in `common/storage/filesystem.go`. Deferred temp-file cleanups are unchanged, as the spec says.\n- Tests: `robustio_test.go` covers succeeding after transient failures, stopping immediately on a non-transient error, and giving up within the bound (using a shortened `timeout`).\n\n**Verification**\n- `make test` passes: Windows amd64 build + vet, then the full suite. The robustio tests also pass with `-race`, and the Windows arm64 build succeeds.\n- `go.mod` is unchanged (`golang.org/x/sys` was already a direct dependency).\n\n**Not verified:** actual retry behavior against a sharing violation. That needs a real Windows host. The Windows predicate is only compile-checked here.\n\n**Known interaction (in spec):** until rdb-207d5c lands, renaming onto an existing read-only object on Windows now waits up to 2s before returning the same \"Access is denied\" error as today."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T07:18:40.049188Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
