{"id":"rdb-e472aa","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a1","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-28T09:54:14.275309Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-bc42f6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Readers keep stale snapshots when another process writes (StateSeq is per-process)","description":"Found while testing rdb-e472aa; reproduces on `main` with the pre-fix code.\n\n## Repro (engine test)\n\n```go\nroot, a := \u003cjournal engine with table t\u003e\nb := engine.OpenWithOptions(ctx, root, journal) // second engine = second process\nexecAll(a, \"INSERT INTO t VALUES (24, 47, 'n2')\")\nqueryIDs(a, \"SELECT id FROM t WHERE n = 'n7'\")   // A resolves \u0026 caches its snapshot\nexecAll(b, \"INSERT INTO t VALUES (13, 2, 'n7')\")  // B commits generation+1\nqueryIDs(a, \"SELECT id FROM t ORDER BY id\")      // [[1] [2] [24]]: row 13 missing, indefinitely\n```\n\n## Cause\n\n`session.resolveSnapshot` (`engine/catalog.go`, added in 864731d, M4.4 overhead work) returns the cached snapshot whenever `repo.StateSeq` equals `db.lastStateSeq`. `StateSeq` is an in-memory `atomic.Uint64` on this process's `repository.Repository` and is only bumped by this process's own commits, checkpoints and publications. Writes by any other engine or process (CLI `repodb commit` next to a running server, two embedded apps, a separate `repodb sync`) never bump it, so the reader keeps serving the old snapshot until it writes itself. Its next write then conflicts as a stale writer.\n\n`TestSeparateJournalEnginesObserveProgressAndRejectStaleWriter` passes only because its reader session never resolved a snapshot before the other engine's commit.\n\n## Fix direction\n\nKeep the fast path, but make its validity check detect changes from other processes cheaply: e.g., the journal file's size/mtime/inode (the journal cache already tracks `info`/`offset`) plus the data ref's value. Add a cross-engine visibility regression test (read, other engine writes, read again) for journal and native-git modes.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a0","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-bc42f6","target_id":"rdb-e472aa","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-09-28T10:07:52.245718Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-e472aa","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T10:14:59.077371Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-e472aa","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-26ce2520-46aa-4266-a8da-7fcb34cfeb49","text":"Implemented; spec updated to match (a cache and repo-wide lint were added).\n\n**Fix**\n- `ensureIndexEdits` derives index edits for persisted index trees from the pending-row overlay (`overlayIndexEdits`); unpersisted indexes keep the full rebuild.\n- A per-generation cache (`database.indexEdits`) is seeded by committing journal transactions and by clean readers, compacted and shared copy-on-append. Without it, a single insert with 10k pending edits took 630 ms; with it, 32 ms (27 ms pre-fix, which was incorrect).\n\n**Tests** (`engine/journal_index_test.go`): insert/update/delete/mixed-index regressions (all failed before the fix), a 150-step model-based test with checkpoints and reopens (fails pre-fix; passes with and without the cache), and `BenchmarkJournalIndexedInsertWithPending`.\n\n**Lint (user request)**: gofmt on 5 files, 8 unused decls removed (U1000), 3 error strings lowercased (ST1005). New `make lint` (gofmt, vet and staticcheck v0.8.1, native + windows) is in the README.\n\n**Verification**: `make test`, `make lint`, race tests, govulncheck, `go mod tidy`: all clean. The binary repro now finds the row via the index and rejects the duplicate.\n\n**New bug found**: rdb-bc42f6, readers keep stale snapshots when another process writes (per-process `StateSeq`). It is pre-existing and out of scope."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T10:14:59.101942Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
