{"id":"rdb-bc42f6","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f0d99f20-f23f-4b09-b389-92c54cbd4376","text":"Implemented per spec (the spec now records the exact trigger and the StateSeq removal).\n\n- `Repository.Head` caches the ref value behind a ref storage stamp (loose ref, packed-refs, reftable/tables.list; stat identity, size, mtime; stamp taken before `rev-parse`). `Current` uses it.\n- `resolveSnapshot` always checks on-disk state: journal → `WorkingState.Current`; native-Git → `Head` plus reuse of the snapshot when the commit is unchanged.\n- The exported `Repository.StateSeq` (and its 6 bumps) and `database.lastStateSeq` are removed.\n\n**Tests**\n- `TestReadersObserveOtherEngineWrites` (journal-dirty, journal-clean, native-git): all three fail pre-fix.\n- `TestHeadObservesExternalRefUpdate`: update-ref, pack-refs, packed update.\n- Two-engine variant of `TestJournalIndexesMatchModel`: fails pre-fix at step 8.\n\n**Real processes**: two `repodb start` servers on one repo, both modes. On main, A reads stale rows and its next insert fails with \"RepoDB data head changed\"; with the fix, A sees C's row immediately and its insert succeeds.\n\n**Cost**: `BenchmarkSQLAutocommitPointRead` goes from ~130–153 µs to ~135–159 µs (+3–5%).\n\n`make test`, race (repository/engine/integration/cmd), `make lint`, `git diff --check`: all pass."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T10:56:13.580502Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-6ae82d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6287a0f4-6b86-4da1-bb0b-a432995f1108","text":"Prep done (2026-09-28), measurement waits for rdb-bc42f6 to merge.\n\n**Environment**: Docker 29.8.0.\n- MySQL `mysql:8.4` (8.4.11): container `repodb-bench-mysql`, 127.0.0.1:3306.\n- Dolt `dolthub/dolt-sql-server:latest` (2.3.5): container `repodb-bench-dolt`, 127.0.0.1:3336.\n\nSmoke runs of `dbbench -mode external` work against both.\n\n**Dolt correctness finding**: concurrent autocommit `UPDATE counter SET value = value + 1` loses acknowledged updates in Dolt 2.3.3, 2.3.4 and 2.3.5. A standalone repro with 4×20 separate connections acknowledged 80 updates and stored 68–71. The harness reports `lost-update check` failures. The 2026-09-13 Dolt JSON already recorded the same failure (120 acknowledged, 40 stored), even though that report claimed all checks passed; the history banner now says so (rdb-ec8ec2).\n\n**Plan**: report Dolt's numbers, but mark `contended_increment` as failing correctness (lost updates) instead of presenting its latency as comparable.\n\n**Harness gaps to close in this issue**:\n1. Record the external server's `VERSION()` in the JSON.\n2. Surface `verification_error` in the printed table so failed-correctness rows can't be quoted as passing."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T11:13:33.898816Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
