{"id":"rdb-586f81","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"updated","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T13:54:51.377425Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-586f81","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-c72f4caa-e9a8-465d-b987-35ab615095d0","text":"Implemented; spec updated with implementation notes.\n\n**Results** (`BenchmarkSQLAutocommitScans`, 50k rows, journal, autocommit):\n\n| query | before | after |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| `WHERE id BETWEEN 25000 AND 25099` | 109 ms | 0.25 ms |\n| `ORDER BY id LIMIT 20` | 96 ms | 0.14 ms |\n| `WHERE id \u003e 49000 ORDER BY id LIMIT 20` | n/a | 0.12 ms |\n| full scan | 88 ms | 67 ms |\n\n**Changes**\n- `engine/keycodec.go`: order-preserving codec.\n- `engine/ranges.go`: interval building, streaming primary and index iterators.\n- `catalog.go`: range dispatch, `CanSupport` shapes, `sql.OrderedIndex`, streaming full scans, dead lookup code removed.\n- Format 1 → 2 (repository and journal).\n- Legacy import refused (`ErrLegacyUnsupported`).\n- Docs: storage-format key-encoding section, guide, README.\n\n**Found along the way**\n- go-mysql-server's `WriteWeightString` is little-endian and not orderable, so the codec uses `Sorter()` weights.\n- `unique_col IS NULL` via the old unique path is fixed.\n\n**Tests:** codec property tests (13 types), a range model test across 3 modes × 4 key types with plan-path assertions, plan tests, and a legacy/format test. End to end: the v1 repo refusal message, and server range queries with negative ints and a DECIMAL index with NULLs. `make test`, race and `make lint` pass.\n\n**Open question for the user:** remove `repodb import-legacy` entirely, or keep it refusing format 1?"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T13:54:51.401766Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
