{"id":"rdb-586f81","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T14:43:36.734903Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-586f81","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2a3bdc02-db68-4530-b32c-fa4aed14f73a","text":"Review revision (user: \"remove the command entirely. this is an alpha there is no legacy\"). Spec updated first.\n\nRemoved all legacy-layout support:\n- the `repodb import-legacy` command and its usage entry;\n- `common/repository/legacy.go` (`ImportLegacy`);\n- the tracked-`.repodb` detection in `Init`/`OpenWithSnapshot`;\n- `ErrLegacyLayout` and `ErrLegacyUnsupported`;\n- the `Repository.Dir` field (only the importer used it);\n- the legacy test section and its helpers (`writeLegacyLayout`, `writeJSON`); the test is renamed `TestAbsentUnsupportedAndCorruptRepositories`;\n- docs: the README command row and docs table, the guide's command row plus both import sections, and the storage-format recovery bullet and import paragraph.\n\n`plan.md` (historical plan) is unchanged.\n\n`make test`, race tests (repository/engine/integration/cmd), `make lint`, the link check and `git diff --check` pass."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T14:48:45.523182Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-586f81","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:01:42.522422Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-586f81","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f4f02a89-8b66-494e-9e41-42161e0b474d","text":"Review fixes (spec updated first):\n\n- **P1, `\u003e MAX` returned the full table.** Confirmed: an exclusive lower bound on an all-`0xFF` key (BIGINT and BIGINT UNSIGNED max) made `keyPrefixEnd` return nil, which as a *start* means \"from the first key\". `lowerCutKey` and `rangeInterval` now report `none`, and `rangeIntervals` drops the interval. `AboveAll` as a lower bound goes through the same `exclusiveStart` helper. Only fixed-width 8-byte keys at their maximum can be all `0xFF`; floats, decimals and strings can't.\n  - New `TestRangeQueriesAtIntegerExtremes`: `\u003e`, `\u003e=`, `\u003c`, `\u003c=` and `BETWEEN` at MIN/MAX for signed and unsigned BIGINT, on the primary key and a secondary index, with a plan-path assertion. Before the fix, `k \u003e MAX` returned every row for both signed and unsigned keys; secondary-index keys were unaffected because the `0x01` marker prevents all-`0xFF`.\n- **P3.** storage-format.md now says the subject is `RepoDB snapshot v\u003cformat version\u003e` (currently v2), matching the code, which derives it from `FormatVersion`.\n\n`make test`, race tests, `make lint` and `git diff --check` pass."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:05:59.571795Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
