{"id":"rdb-2483e8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Allow users to make an immutable historical snapshot the active read context for repeated CLI, embedded, or server reads without moving or rewriting a named data branch.\n\nProvide an explicit detached/read-only mode, reject switching when current working changes are not safely preserved, and require creation of a named data branch before accepting writes. Status output must make detached state unmistakable and show the source snapshot. Switching back must restore the branch’s own journal and conflict state.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-3a56dc","sort_order":"aX","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Check out a historical snapshot as detached data state"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:46:45.02443Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
