{"id":"rdb-931f20","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"rdb-931f20","target_id":"rdb-4c3ae3"},{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"rdb-931f20","target_id":"rdb-df092b"}],"description":"The docs/ tree mixes current behavior with milestone contracts (M0–M4), a superseded implementation plan, prototype write-ups and dated performance results. These describe past, now-invalid state and keep misleading agents and readers.\n\nTarget:\n- docs/ describes the **current** state only: CLI usage, architecture, Go library usage, the supported SQL surface, and the benchmark methodology.\n- `docs/benchmarks/latest.md` is the only performance record.\n- The Exponential backlog is the roadmap. The README roadmap summarizes it without issue IDs, with concurrent writers under \"Now\".\n- Historical design rationale lives in xpo specs and walkthroughs, and in git history.","estimate":5,"labels":["task","docs"],"sort_order":"a7","status":"PLANNED","title":"Docs describe current state only: CLI, architecture, Go library; retire plans and milestone docs"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:04:19.437141Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-931f20","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"created","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:04:43.865002Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-f4dec8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"rdb-f4dec8","target_id":"rdb-931f20"}],"description":"rdb-931f20 removes the milestone docs, but code for the milestone experiments remains:\n- `experiments/gitstorage` (`make m0`);\n- `experiments/m2bench` (`make m2-bench`);\n- the `m4.2-bench` and `m4.3-bench` Makefile targets.\n\nDecide for each whether it still measures something current (keep it, rename it, and document it in `docs/testing.md` or `docs/benchmark.md`) or whether `dbbench` and the Go benchmarks have superseded it (delete it). Agents should not find milestone-named entry points that suggest current workflows.","labels":["task"],"sort_order":"ae","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Review legacy experiments and milestone Makefile targets (gitstorage, m2bench, m0/m2/m4.x-bench)"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:06:53.905718Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
