{"id":"rdb-c56142","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"dependencies":null,"labels":null,"sort_order":"a0V","status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:12:57.068038Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"rdb-53214c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"rdb-53214c","target_id":"rdb-931f20"}],"description":"Found while documenting (rdb-931f20); reproduced.\n\n## Repro\n\nIn journal mode (the `engine.Open` default):\n1. `CREATE TABLE t (id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY, v TEXT)`\n2. `Checkpoint(\"create\")`\n3. `INSERT INTO t VALUES (1,'a'),(2,'b')`\n\n`WorkingState.Status` then reports `Dirty=true, Generation=2`, but `WorkingState.Diff` returns an empty list. `repodb diff` therefore prints \"No uncommitted data changes.\" while `repodb status` says the working state is dirty.\n\n## Cause\n\nJournal transactions record typed row edits (`CommitTypedEdits`). `applyTypedEditsToSnapshot` keeps them as pending edits beside the base manifest and changes the manifest only for schema changes and drops, so the table's `DataRoot` is unchanged. `Diff` compares manifest table entries (`before.Equal(after)`), so a table whose only changes are row edits looks unchanged.\n\n## Fix direction\n\n`Diff` also reports tables that have pending row edits (from `PendingTableEdits` or the view's pending map), as `modified`, or `added` when the table is new since the base. Optionally include per-table counts of inserted, updated and deleted keys.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A test covers row-only changes to an existing table (insert, update, delete) and checks `Diff` lists the table.\n- The CLI's `repodb diff` agrees with `repodb status` about whether anything is uncommitted.","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"ad","status":"BACKLOG","title":"repodb diff reports no changes for journal row edits to existing tables"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:13:38.266834Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-53214c","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"dependencies":null,"labels":null,"sort_order":"Zz","status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:13:53.272737Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"rdb-ff5432","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"rdb-ff5432","target_id":"rdb-931f20"}],"description":"Found while verifying the SQL surface for rdb-931f20; reproduced.\n\n## Repro (embedded, journal mode)\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE t (id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY, v VARCHAR(20), n INT);\nSTART TRANSACTION READ ONLY;   -- succeeds\nINSERT INTO t VALUES (99,'ro',0);\n```\n\nThe `INSERT` panics and kills the process:\n\n```\npanic: runtime error: invalid memory address or nil pointer dereference\ngithub.com/dolthub/go-mysql-server/sql/analyzer.validateReadOnlyTransaction.func1\n\tsql/analyzer/validation_rules.go:921\n...\ngithub.com/nicbet/repodb/engine.(*Session).Query  engine/engine.go:492\n```\n\n## Likely cause\n\nRepoDB's transaction sets `readOnly` (`engine/catalog.go`, `IsReadOnly()`), so go-mysql-server's `validateReadOnlyTransaction` rule inspects the plan. At `validation_rules.go:921` it dereferences something RepoDB's table or database leaves nil, for example a table's database or a `sql.Databaser`. Confirm which accessor returns nil.\n\n## Impact\n\n- **Embedded:** a crash of the host application.\n- **Server:** likely a crash of `repodb start`, unless go-mysql-server recovers the handler panic. Verify over the wire.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A write inside a read-only transaction returns MySQL's read-only transaction error (`ER_CANT_EXECUTE_IN_READ_ONLY_TRANSACTION`, 1792) without panicking, both embedded and over the wire.\n- Reads inside read-only transactions still work.\n- Regression tests cover both.","labels":["bug"],"priority":1,"sort_order":"ad","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Write inside START TRANSACTION READ ONLY panics (nil pointer in read-only validation)"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:15:46.353734Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-5f12a3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"rdb-5f12a3","target_id":"rdb-931f20"},{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"rdb-5f12a3","target_id":"rdb-8b1539"}],"description":"Found while verifying the SQL surface for rdb-931f20. Each item was reproduced against an embedded engine at `540737d` unless marked otherwise. Each statement or option succeeds, but RepoDB doesn't do what it says. The fix for each is either to honor it or to reject it with a clear error.\n\n- [ ] **Views are session-local and silently lost.** `CREATE VIEW v1 AS SELECT id FROM t` succeeds, but another session gets `table not found: v1`, as does the same session after a reopen. The database doesn't implement `sql.ViewDatabase`, so go-mysql-server keeps the view in the session's in-memory registry. Fix: persist views, or reject `CREATE VIEW`.\n- [ ] **A JSON primary key is accepted but unusable.** `CREATE TABLE j (id JSON PRIMARY KEY)` succeeds; every insert then fails with `column type json cannot be part of a key`. Validate key column types at `CREATE TABLE`, `ALTER TABLE` and `CREATE INDEX` time. (A JSON secondary index is already rejected by go-mysql-server.)\n- [ ] **Index prefix lengths are ignored.** `CREATE INDEX pre ON t (v(5))` succeeds and indexes the whole column: `SHOW INDEX` reports no `Sub_part`, and `PrefixLengths()` returns nil. For a UNIQUE index this changes semantics, since uniqueness applies to the full value rather than the prefix. Fix: reject prefix lengths, or implement them.\n- [ ] **TIME(n) precision is dropped.** `CREATE TABLE tm (id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY, x TIME(3))` is shown as `x time` by `SHOW CREATE TABLE` immediately. `encodeSchema` persists precision only for DATE/DATETIME/TIMESTAMP, and `decodeType` always returns `types.Time`. Fix: persist and honor it, or reject a non-zero precision.\n- [ ] **`repodb-server --database` and `server.Config.DatabaseName` do nothing.** The value is defaulted in `server.New` but never passed to the engine, so the database is always the manifest's `DefaultDatabase` (`repodb`). Found by code reading; not run. Fix: apply it, or remove the flag and field.\n- [ ] **A FULLTEXT index gives a garbled error.** `CREATE FULLTEXT INDEX ft ON t (v)` returns `tables cannot be created on database %!s(MISSING)`. Fix: return a clear \"FULLTEXT indexes are not supported\".\n- [ ] **Minor: `ALTER TABLE t DROP PRIMARY KEY`'s error has a formatting artifact** (`error: table is not primary key alterable%!(EXTRA *plan.ResolvedTable=…)`). This comes from go-mysql-server; wrap it if practical.\n\nThe acceptance criterion for each item is a test proving the statement is either honored or rejected with a clear error. `docs/sql.md` states the current behavior until each is fixed.","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"ae","status":"BACKLOG","title":"DDL and server options accepted but not honored (views, JSON keys, prefix indexes, TIME(n), --database)"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:15:46.385656Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-ff5432","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"dependencies":null,"labels":null,"sort_order":"Zy","status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:16:20.036114Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"rdb-5f12a3","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"ZyV","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:16:22.951178Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"rdb-4c3ae3","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Position RepoDB as a relational database that users can clone, query, branch, modify, inspect, merge, and synchronize through Git—whether or not the repository contains application code.\n\nThis roadmap begins after the current Tier 1 implementation and performance work establishes a credible supported workload envelope. It deliberately separates table-stakes adoption work from the differentiated version-control experience.\n\n## Product outcome\n\nRepoDB supports two complementary deployment modes:\n\n1. Embedded/local-first applications with explicit Git synchronization.\n2. A securely operated standalone MySQL-compatible server backed by the same cloneable, versioned data history.\n\n## Roadmap outcomes\n\n- Historical snapshots, diffs, named data branches, switching, merging, restore, and revert are first-class operations.\n- Standalone network service has secure defaults, authentication, TLS, authorization, and operational controls.\n- Common applications can rely on generated keys, referential integrity, and a tested compatibility profile.\n- Backup, recovery, compaction, format migration, and history maintenance make long-lived repositories operable.\n\n## Sequencing\n\n1. Finish Tier 1 performance/scalability work and publish the supported envelope:\n   - reverse index scans (rdb-acd36d);\n   - fewer Git subprocesses per sync (rdb-2c93ca);\n   - workload profiling (rdb-db5459);\n   - **local write coordination for concurrent sessions (rdb-df092b)**: per-key conflicts, group commit, safe autocommit retry, MySQL-compatible conflict errors. The standalone server should not claim general OLTP concurrency before this lands.\n2. Establish snapshot-addressing and operational foundations.\n3. Deliver historical inspection and secure standalone access.\n4. Add data branching/merge workflows and broader application compatibility.\n5. Harden long-lived operation and publish a standalone deployment profile.\n\nChild stories remain BACKLOG until explicitly planned and specified. The README roadmap summarizes this sequencing without issue IDs; keep them in step.\n\n## Critical paths\n\nThe strict version-control critical path is:\n\n```\nrdb-7b1006  Snapshot addressing\n    ↓\nrdb-33692c  Named data branches\n    ↓\nrdb-23dce8  Safe branch switching\n    ↓\nrdb-e35ef0  Branch merging\n    ↓\nrdb-9bbd62  Commit revert\n```\n\nParallel after `rdb-7b1006`:\n\n- `rdb-ce14fb` — History/log\n- `rdb-71f167` — Historical queries\n- `rdb-493758` — Row/schema diffs\n- `rdb-2483e8` — Detached historical checkout\n\nOther critical tracks:\n\n```\nSecure server:\nrdb-d0b39d → rdb-5720c1 → rdb-8d63a3\nconfiguration → auth/TLS → authorization\n\nApplication compatibility:\nrdb-a2d28e ─┐\n             ├→ rdb-65b203 → rdb-8b1539\nrdb-48af2f ─┘\nAUTO_INCREMENT + foreign keys → metadata → compatibility profile\n\nConcurrent writers (step 1):\nrdb-40ba7c ─┬→ rdb-eb6674\nrdb-8f75fc  └→ rdb-1d7fab\nper-key conflicts + group commit → autocommit retry, MySQL errors\n```\n\nThe best first post-performance issue is `rdb-7b1006`; it unlocks nearly the entire differentiated version-control track.","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:23:32.743677Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-f4dec8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-165bdd8f-dd9e-47e7-afd0-4bca699441d5","text":"More leftovers found while documenting the current architecture (rdb-931f20). Review these together with the experiments:\n- `common/storage` filesystem store (`storage.Filesystem`): used only by its own tests. The runtime reads objects from Git (`cat-file --batch`) and keeps them in memory.\n- `Repository.CacheDir()` (`\u003ccommon-dir\u003e/repodb/cache/v\u003cformat\u003e`): defined but nothing writes to it.\n- `common/query`: used only by its own smoke test.\n- User-visible error messages still name milestones:\n  - `RepoDB M2 requires an explicit PRIMARY KEY`\n  - `unsupported M2 SQL type \u003cX\u003e`\n  - `column \u003cc\u003e uses unsupported M2 schema behavior`\n  - `RepoDB M2 does not support savepoints`\n\n  `docs/sql.md` quotes them verbatim, so update it if they change.\n- The `WorkingState` doc comment calls it \"the opt-in M4.3 durable journal prototype\", and `CommitTypedEdits` refers to \"the M4.4 compact persistence path\". Journal persistence is the library default."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:23:47.421976Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-931f20","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-5fe012ae-aa70-4bbc-86c3-28e53370660c","text":"Ready for review.\n\n**docs/ now contains only current-state documents:**\n- `cli.md`: every `repodb` command and flag, persistence modes, sync, conflicts, backup, Git command behavior;\n- `library.md`: engine, sessions, transactions, commit outcomes and recovery, checkpoints, the sync API, server, client. All 9 code blocks compile against the module;\n- `sql.md`: the verified SQL surface, with every unsupported feature citing its backlog issue;\n- `architecture.md`: packages, where state lives, snapshot format, Prolly trees, key and row encodings, reads, both persistence modes, concurrency limits, sync and merge, durability and recovery, Git integration, platforms;\n- `testing.md`: per-suite coverage of behaviors, test infrastructure, fuzz targets, benchmarks, how to measure coverage, and known gaps;\n- `benchmark.md`: methodology, with publishing now replace-in-place;\n- `benchmarks/latest.md`.\n\n**Removed:** plan, guide, sql-m2, storage-format, working-state, sync-m3, merge-m4, git-integration, fuzz-testing, and `benchmarks/history/` (48.5k lines, mostly history JSON).\n\n**Other changes:**\n- README: new docs table, roadmap (Done / Now / Next, no IDs, concurrent writers under Now), links and contributing rewritten.\n- `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`: a \"Documentation\" section outside the managed xpo blocks.\n- Roadmap epic rdb-4c3ae3: step 1 now includes rdb-df092b, plus its critical path.\n\n**Checks:**\n- links and anchors resolve (script);\n- all 19 cited issue IDs are open;\n- no milestone or prototype wording except verbatim error strings;\n- CLI commands and flags match `main.go` (script);\n- `make lint` passes.\n\n**Filed while verifying:**\n- rdb-53214c: diff misses row edits (reproduced);\n- rdb-ff5432: a write in a READ ONLY transaction crashes the process (reproduced; priority 1);\n- rdb-5f12a3: accepted-but-not-honored DDL and options (reproduced except `--database`, which was found by reading the code);\n- a comment on rdb-8f75fc (group commit exists but can't batch);\n- a comment on rdb-f4dec8 (dead code and milestone error strings)."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:24:34.326656Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
