{"id":"rdb-5f12a3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-cef9be63-6af2-4b2a-915a-28d19d8be9f7","text":"Ready for review. All seven items are handled; `make test` and `make lint` pass.\n\n| Item | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| Views | rejected: `views are not supported (rdb-5c1808)`; feature filed as rdb-5c1808 (BACKLOG) |\n| JSON key | `CREATE TABLE … JSON PRIMARY KEY` rejected by RepoDB; every other JSON key case was already rejected by go-mysql-server |\n| Prefix lengths | rejected in `CREATE INDEX`, `ADD INDEX`, inline `INDEX`, and `PRIMARY KEY (v(n))` (via `IndexedTableCreator`) |\n| `TIME(n)` | precision persisted, in both modes and across reopen |\n| `--database` | flag and `server.Config.DatabaseName` removed |\n| FULLTEXT | go-mysql-server's `table does not support FULLTEXT indexes` instead of the garbled error |\n| `ADD`/`DROP PRIMARY KEY` | rejected with a clear message |\n\n**Departures from the first spec (spec updated):**\n- No JSON key checks in `CreateIndex` or `ModifyColumn`, because go-mysql-server rejects those cases first. A test keeps `keyable` in step with the key codec instead.\n- The FULLTEXT message is go-mysql-server's own, not a custom RepoDB one.\n\n**Files:**\n- rejections: `engine/unsupported.go`;\n- key-type check: `engine/keycodec.go`;\n- `TIME` precision: `engine/catalog.go`;\n- tests: `engine/ddl_honored_test.go` and `TestKeyableMatchesStoredTypes`."},"created_at":"2026-10-01T11:33:53.1156Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
