{"id":"rdb-e0c717","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a0","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-10-01T12:00:28.733263Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-ed0738","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"A rejected COMMIT leaves the session on the dead transaction; retries fail","description":"Found while implementing rdb-e0c717; reproduced.\n\n## Repro (native-git, two engines)\n\n```sql\n-- s2\nSTART TRANSACTION;\nINSERT INTO t VALUES (2);\n-- s1 (other engine) commits INSERT INTO t VALUES (1)\nCOMMIT;                        -- RepoDB data head changed (ErrConflict), as documented\nSELECT * FROM t;               -- [[2]]: the failed transaction's own row\nINSERT INTO t VALUES (2);      -- duplicate primary key\n```\n\nAn autocommit statement whose commit is rejected behaves the same way. After rdb-e0c717, that includes `ErrWorkingStateDirty`; the next query fails with `snapshot writer is already committed`.\n\n## Cause\n\ngo-mysql-server clears the session's transaction (`ctx.SetTransaction(nil)`, `SetIgnoreAutoCommit(false)`) only after `CommitTransaction` succeeds. RepoDB's transaction can't be committed twice, because its writer is single-use. So after a failed commit the session keeps a dead transaction with its unpublished edits. `docs/sql.md` tells applications to retry the whole transaction, but the retry runs inside the dead one.\n\n## Fix\n\nWhen `session.CommitTransaction` fails, clear the transaction and leave explicit-transaction mode, like MySQL rolling back after a failed commit. The next statement starts a fresh transaction on the current snapshot.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- After a rejected `COMMIT` (and a rejected autocommit statement), the session sees only published data and a retry succeeds.\n- Covered in native-git and journal modes.\n\nFixed in the rdb-e0c717 branch, because that issue's acceptance (retry after a checkpoint) depends on it.","status":"DOING","sort_order":"a1","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@MBPM1X.local\u003e","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-ed0738","target_id":"rdb-e0c717","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-10-01T12:03:59.524355Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-e0c717","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-01T12:10:04.045867Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-e0c717","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-da53e262-9ddf-4ce3-996b-b1eb5b672b46","text":"Ready for review.\n\n**Reproduced first.**\n- Sync: a journal commit in the window gave `fast-forwarded-local`. The journal engine kept accepting writes, its checkpoint failed forever, and fresh opens failed with `ErrWorkingBaseChanged`.\n- Native-git commits under a dirty journal also moved the head. This path is new, found while investigating.\n\n**Fix (publication layer).** Every update of `refs/repodb/data` takes `working.lock` → `publish.lock`. While the journal is dirty, all publications except a checkpoint fail with `ErrWorkingStateDirty`:\n- native-git commits;\n- sync's fast-forward and merge (reported as `ErrWorkingDirty`).\n\nThe dirty check is a cached scan of new journal record kinds (one `stat` when unchanged). `BenchmarkSQLWriteBatches` shows no change.\n\n**Recovery.** `ErrWorkingBaseChanged` now names the journal base, the head and the new `docs/cli.md#recovering-a-stranded-journal` section: reset the ref, checkpoint, sync. A test proves it brings back every row.\n\n**Also fixed: rdb-ed0738** (filed, linked). A rejected `COMMIT` left the session on the dead transaction, so retries failed. This applied even to plain `ErrConflict`, despite the docs saying to retry.\n\n**Tests:**\n- sync race (fast-forward and merge) through a `beforePublish` test hook;\n- native-git under a dirty journal;\n- a concurrent journal/native/checkpoint loop (also under `-race`);\n- the recovery procedure;\n- rejected-commit retry in both modes.\n\n`make test` and `make lint` pass. Docs updated in architecture, cli, library, sql and testing."},"created_at":"2026-10-01T12:10:04.077486Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-ed0738","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-11556563-24dd-4f44-b635-d9105065dc0c","text":"Fixed in the rdb-e0c717 branch. `session.CommitTransaction` clears the transaction (`SetTransaction(nil)`) and explicit-transaction mode (`SetIgnoreAutoCommit(false)`) when the commit fails. `TestRejectedCommitStartsFreshTransaction` (`engine/working_test.go`) covers native-git and journal: after a rejected `COMMIT` the session sees only published rows, and the retried transaction commits. It fails without the fix. `docs/sql.md` states that a failed `COMMIT` ends the transaction."},"created_at":"2026-10-01T12:10:04.104873Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
